WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.360
A horse and a donkey can mate.

2
00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:06.260
Their offspring is a mule,
and a mule is sterile.

3
00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:11.140
So biologists count the horse and
the donkey as 2 separate species.

4
00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.410
Now picture one population
of beetles on a plain.

5
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.730
A river cuts the plain in two,
and the groups never meet again.

6
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:23.260
How do two groups that never meet
again end up as different species?

7
00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.700
In this mission, you'll pin
down what counts as a species,

8
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.040
and where that definition struggles.

9
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:33.100
Then you'll read an experiment in which
fly populations were kept in separate

10
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.910
cages for 100 generations.

11
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:41.330
Your mission: explain how two groups
that never meet again become two species.
